  message: "Premise re-check 2026-10-25 on dev 9245df71d6 (production-CLI repros on tiny fixtures, scratchpad stale1025b/repro_<ID>/). CURRENT for all 29 named rows (ledger io_primitive_kinds.py:194-223 = objc 21 + kotlin 5 + swift 3; size pin tests/test_io_primitive_kinds.py:151); the boundary blocker stands (objc NSMutableURLRequest requestWithURL: still net_send, NSFetchRequest fetchRequestWithEntityName: still db_read). Fixtures: ObjC class messages are stamped method with the class in the module slot and classify (NSData/NSString/NSDate/NSTask), supporting 're-kind is classification-neutral' for objc (re-kind A/B not run). Kotlin File(p).readText()/readLines()/readBytes() reach java.io.File rows and nothing emits kotlin.io.FilesKt, so the 5 facade rows (kotlin.yaml:103-110) are dead -> DELETE them (kotlin.io.ConsoleKt :154 is the function-kind precedent). Swift Date.now and ProcessInfo.processInfo emit no edge at all (unreachable as any kind); DispatchTime.now() classifies. REMAINDER UNDERCOUNTED and the ledger is no longer the complete record ADR-0059 §3 calls it: ff7defd603 (INV-vamif, 2026-09-27) added class-method launchers under methods: after the ledger was pinned -- objc launchedTaskWithLaunchPath:arguments: and launchedTaskWithExecutableURL:arguments:error:terminationHandler: (objc.yaml:235-236), swift Process.launchedProcess (swift.yaml:165). Reached both ways: swift Process.run (:163), objc NSDate timeIntervalSinceReferenceDate (:254). Likely mis-named, not checked against Apple docs: swift FileHandle.fileHandleFor{Reading,Writing,Updating} (:48, :74-75) and InputStream.inputStreamWithFileAtPath (:54) -- Swift imports these as initializers; FileHandle(forReadingAtPath:) emits swift:external:FileHandle and classifies nothing (a recall gap). Also seen: swift stamps method on Type.static() (INV-tanom shape; no item searched). P3 kept: classification impact nil/near-nil, but the ledger's completeness claim is now false -- add the unledgered rows or make the ledger check catch new ones."  # d60c
